<text xml:lang="ta" type="edition">
  <body>
      <div rend="parallel"> 
        <p xml:id="Aink183-kilavi">
         varaiviṭaivaittup pirintuḻi āṟṟāḷākiya talaimakaḷ mālaikkuc colliyatu.</p>    <p xml:lang="en">
          Spoken by the heroine to the evening as one who could not bear it, when [he] separated, putting a hold on [their] marriage.</p>
    </div>   
    <div rend="parallel">
      <lg xml:id="Aink183">
<l>kaṇaṅko ḷaruvik kāṉkeḻu nāṭaṉ</l>
<l>kuṟumpoṟai nāṭa ṉalvaya lūraṉ</l>
<l>ṟaṇkaṭaṟ cērppaṉ pirinteṉap paṇṭaiyiṟ</l>
<l>kaṭumpakal varuti kaiyaṟu mālai</l>
<l>koṭuṅkaḻi neytaluṅ kūmpak</l>
<l>kālai variṉuṅ kaḷaiñarō vilarē</l>
      </lg>
      <lg xml:lang="en">
        <l>Since the man of the land that has forests [with] groups of waterfalls,</l>
        <l>The man of the land with small hills, the man of the town with good paddy fields </l>
        <l>[And] the man from the cool seashore has separated [from me], </l>
        <l>You come in this harsh midday, like earlier.</l>
        <l>Even if you had come in the day, as the Neytal flowers of the desolate evening</l>
        <l>In the curved backwaters, close,</l>
        <l>You are not the one to remove [my sorrow]. </l>
              </lg>
    </div>
  </body>
</text>
